# claude: this fork never had a .gitignore at all - same gap as the
# sibling forks/arm-pi1/forks/arm-pi2 forks. Covers both the
# real-hardware build outputs (kernel7.bin/kernel.list/kernel.map/
# build/) and the additive QEMU-only ones this repo's own bring-up
# added (kernel7-qemu.bin/kernel-qemu.map/build-qemu//armstub64.bin).
# Root-anchored (leading "/") and by exact name, deliberately NOT a
# broad "*.bin"/"*.img" glob - source/font.bin/font1.bin are genuine
# checked-in binary assets (font bitmap data, not build output) and a
# recursive glob would have caught those too.
#
# source/fs.img WAS checked in here too, until 2026-09-09: it is the
# OUTPUT of uprogs/'s own build (mkfs plus every UPROGS binary), and the
# Makefile now regenerates it on every build (see its
# "source/fs.img: uprogs-fs-img" rule) rather than trusting a committed
# blob to stay in step with uprogs/*.c. Same treatment as the siblings
# forks/arm-pi1 and forks/arm-pi2. What the committed copy was hiding
# here was worse than a stale build: uprogs/ did not compile at all
# (CFLAGS asked for an FPU-less -march against a hard-float toolchain
# default), and once it did, the current usertests binary no longer FIT
# the filesystem - so the blob had been supplying an older, smaller
# usertests than uprogs/*.c would produce, and every "ALL TESTS PASSED"
# for this port was testing that stale binary. See include/fs.h's own
# NDIRECT comment.
/build/
/build-qemu/
/kernel7.bin
/kernel7-qemu.bin
/armstub64.bin
/kernel.list
/kernel.map
/kernel-qemu.map
/source/fs.img
